-- Seed data for local/dev testing of the film catalog UI.
-- videoFileId / trailerUrl are placeholder strings only, not real B2 objects - playback for these
-- seeded episodes will show a "video not found" state, which is expected.
-- Runs on every startup (spring.sql.init.mode=always); INSERT IGNORE / NOT EXISTS keep it idempotent.
-- NOTE: this file mirrors the live dev DB as of 2026-08-07, after a full cast-accuracy audit: every
-- film_cast row was checked against its film's own description (or well-known real casting) and
-- corrected where wrong - not just the films that had 0/1 cast rows. Notable fixes: Vagabond had
-- leftover cast from the placeholder film it replaced (now Lee Seung-gi/Bae Suzy/Shin Sung-rok);
-- Wicked: For Good had Matthew McConaughey mislabeled as Elphaba (now Cynthia Erivo); Spider-Man:
-- Brand New Day had Robert Downey Jr. as "Tony Stark/Spider-Mentor" (now Tom Holland); Phu Nhân Đại
-- Quân and Tiếng yêu này anh dịch được không? had actors that contradicted their own description text.
-- Na Tra 2's only cast row (Wu Lei) couldn't be verified and was removed rather than left wrong.
-- Unused directors/actors are deleted as they stop being referenced by any film. Several Chinese
-- donghua titles still have 0 cast - no confident real voice-cast data was available, so they were
-- left alone rather than guessed. Vagabond (16 eps) and Diên Hy Công Lược (70 eps) episode counts
-- were corrected to match reality. Multi-director support: films.director_id was replaced by a
-- film_director join table, mirroring film_cast. Director/actor avatar_url and film thumbnail_url
-- for upload-managed images are intentionally left NULL - they're resolved fresh from *_file_id at
-- read time (see resolveAvatar/resolveThumbnail), so the raw presigned URL briefly returned by the
-- upload endpoint isn't worth seeding.

-- Directors (avatar_url left NULL on purpose - add photos later)

-- Actors (avatar_url left NULL on purpose - add photos later)

-- Films

-- Film genres (element collection, no primary key -> guard with NOT EXISTS)
SELECT * FROM (SELECT 'f1111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111' AS film_id, 'SCI_FI' AS genre) t
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM film_genres WHERE film_id = 'f1111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111' AND genre = 'SCI_FI');
